; widenprobe.tal - settle two things by measurement, not by reading the source.
;
;   1. Does @widen sign-extend, or shift the byte into the high half?
;   2. Are GTH2 and LTH2 first-then-second, or second-then-first?
;
; Both are load-bearing for @seg, and getting either backwards is a silent wrong
; answer rather than a crash: a wrong @widen still returns a short, and a
; reversed comparison still returns a flag.
;
; The answer is read off the picture. A widened $ff that is -1 lands off the
; left edge of a 320-wide screen; $ff00 lands off the right. And each
; comparison marks a row only if it came out true, so a row with nothing on it
; is a false and a row with a pixel at x=1 is a true.

INCLUDE "../asm/common.tal"

; common.tal uses $10 to $26; $27 is free.
@ZP.row   = $27                      ; a SHORT, not a byte

@draw
        JSR2 @clear

        ; ---- @widen.  Row 8, x = the widened value.
        LIT2 $0000
        STA2 $ZP.row
        LIT $ff
        JSR2 @widen
        JSR2 @mark

        ; ---- 2 GTH 1, row 9.
        LIT2 $0009
        STA2 $ZP.row
        LIT2 $0002
        LIT2 $0001
        GTH2
        JNZ @g21
        JMP @n21
@g21
        LIT2 $0001
        JSR2 @mark
@n21

        ; ---- 1 GTH 2, row 10.
        LIT2 $000a
        STA2 $ZP.row
        LIT2 $0001
        LIT2 $0002
        GTH2
        JNZ @g12
        JMP @n12
@g12
        LIT2 $0001
        JSR2 @mark
@n12

        ; ---- 2 LTH 1, row 11.
        LIT2 $000b
        STA2 $ZP.row
        LIT2 $0002
        LIT2 $0001
        LTH2
        JNZ @l21
        JMP @n21b
@l21
        LIT2 $0001
        JSR2 @mark
@n21b

        ; ---- 1 LTH 2, row 12.
        LIT2 $000c
        STA2 $ZP.row
        LIT2 $0001
        LIT2 $0002
        LTH2
        JNZ @l12
        JMP @n12b
@l12
        LIT2 $0001
        JSR2 @mark
@n12b

        JMP2r2

; Stack: a short. Plots it at x = the value, y = $ZP.row.
;
; JSR2 and not the JMP2 tail call that @plotat uses: the tail call eats a
; return address of its own, and @plot's own JMP2r2 eats a second one, so a
; routine entered with JSR2 and ending in JMP2 @plot pops two addresses per
; call and lands somewhere the assembler never checked.
@mark
        LDA2 $ZP.row
        LIT $01
        JSR2 @plot
        JMP2r2
